  "headline": "Three road security personnel killed in Hama countryside, Syria",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Three road security personnel were killed on Tuesday in an attack by unidentified gunmen in the Hama countryside of central Syria, according to the North Press Agency. A security source told Syria’s Al-Ikhbariya TV that security forces have been mobilized to investigate the incident and pursue those involved. As of the report, no official statement had been issued by the Internal Security Forces."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "headline": "Police escort Chittagong University Vice-Chancellor and JCD leaders out after 30-hour confinement",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "On the evening of October 13, 2026, police escorted Prof Sheikh Mohammad Shariful Alam, the newly appointed vice-chancellor of Chittagong University of Engineering and Technology (CUET) in Bangladesh, out of his office following a 30-hour confinement. Current and former leaders of Jatiyatabadi Chhatra Dal, who had been trapped in the administrative building with the vice-chancellor since noon on October 12, 2026, were also escorted out during the operation. At 6:15 p.m., Chattogram Deputy Commissioner Zahidul Islam Mia and Superintendent of Police in Chattogram Masud Alam entered the building after students opened the gates and brought the vice-chancellor out. The vice-chancellor was subsequently taken away in an ambulance while approximately 150 protesting students chanted slogans and reiterated demands for the reinstatement of former vice-chancellor Prof Abu Sadat Mohammad Sayem. The students, who have been demonstrating for 21 days, had also cut power and water supplies to the building. Demonstrators stated that the vice-chancellor was permitted to leave only on the condition that he would not return to the campus."
    },
    {
      "text": "During the confinement, the vice-chancellor's health was a central concern. At approximately 11:00 a.m. on October 13, 2026, he reported experiencing chest pain and a headache. At 1:30 p.m., a medical team led by university Medical Centre doctor Shahabuddin examined him, finding his blood pressure to be normal despite discomfort and sweating caused by the lack of electricity and water. Addressing the crowd via megaphone, Deputy Commissioner Zahidul Islam Mia stated that the administration intervened after the vice-chancellor reported feeling unwell due to hypertension and excessive sweating from the heat during his long confinement."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "headline": "Israel returns 22 ancient artefacts to Greece",
  "pages": [
    {
      "text": "Israel returned 22 ancient artefacts to Greece on Tuesday, according to Arab News. The items, which include a statue, drinking vessels, and vases, were described by Greek Culture Minister Lina Mendoni as having been “illegally removed” from Greece. The artefacts, which were seized by Israel Antiquities Authority investigators, date primarily to the fifth and sixth centuries BC. The handover took place at a museum in Athens and was conducted by Israel’s ambassador in Athens, Pninat Yanay. Mendoni stated that this is the first time Israel has returned antiquities to Greece and characterized the event as a gesture of “particular significance” that marks the beginning of closer cooperation between the two nations regarding the protection of cultural heritage."
    }
  ]
}
